{"text": "thirty", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">thirty</i>, metathetic alternant of Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">thriti</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">\u00feritti\u021d</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">\u00fer\u012bti\u0121</i> (\u201cthirty\u201d), from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*\u00fer\u012bz tigiwiz</i> (\u201cthirty\u201d, literally \u201cthree tens\u201d), equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">three</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-ty</i>. Cognate with Scots <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"sco\">therty</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"sco\">tretty</i> (\u201cthirty\u201d), West Frisian <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fy\">tritich</i> (\u201cthirty\u201d), Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">dertig</i> (\u201cthirty\u201d), German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">drei\u00dfig</i> (\u201cthirty\u201d).\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "(slang) A rack of thirty beers.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["General American", "/\u02c8\u03b8\u025dti/"], ["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8\u03b8\u025c\u02d0ti/"]]}